&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50293196</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:53:34 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Show HN: Sheetgraph, AI agents can understand complex spreadsheets</title><link>https://github.com/asharma327/sheetgraph</link><description>&lt;p&gt;Hi guys,&lt;p&gt;I built a tool www.lovespreadsheets.com earlier this year and a huge problem we kept running into is processing messy, real-world, complex spreadsheets for AI agents.&lt;p&gt;Even a "medium" sized spreadsheet converts to about 1m+ tokens if read fully, which immediately blows up the current context windows of most models. So I noticed most agents sample data from spreadsheets in chunks instead.&lt;p&gt;So I (&amp; Claude) built this library Sheetgraph, &lt;a href="https://github.com/asharma327/sheetgraph" rel="nofollow"&gt;https://github.com/asharma327/sheetgraph&lt;/a&gt;, to compress spreadsheets (~100x compression) while still maintaining their structure (like a dependency graph for formulas) &amp; other relevant metadata such as macros, cell data types, formatting. There is a zipped full workbook of the spreadsheet as well for the agent to lookup data as needed.&lt;p&gt;Still rough around the edges so would love any feedback on both the idea and any details. This is used in our primary product + services platform Love Spreadsheets so we are actively maintaining and improving it.&lt;p&gt;Thanks!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
