&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 1&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50292620</guid><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:18:21 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Ask HN: How are you using AI in your personal life?</title><link>https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50292611</link><description>&lt;p&gt;In the latest Stratechery article, Ben says "I’ve created a bunch of different apps to manage my house and sports viewing," and I instantly felt FOMO. I have no idea what his apps could be doing, but I was just wondering what time saving / efficiency capturing ideas are out there that I might be missing out on.&lt;p&gt;I can start with a few that I can think of, but would love to hear more:&lt;p&gt;I recently used AI to navigate a rezoning process in my city (developers are building right behind my property line). It ended up being extremely helpful navigating the labyrinth of local zoning laws and city council actually approved 15 of my requests.&lt;p&gt;I teach a youth group and have very little time to prepare lessons, but I can usually dump in an outline of a lesson and tell my AI to "make it clean and presentable" and it gives me polished slides that help engage the teenagers.&lt;p&gt;What else is out there that I can be doing?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
